# Error Pages

Use the shared `ErrorPage` shell for consistent error UX.

## Component

- `@/components/errors/error-page` → `ErrorPage`

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `app/error.tsx` | Root route error boundary (`reset` + home) |
| `app/global-error.tsx` | Root layout crash (must include `html`/`body`) |
| `app/not-found.tsx` | 404 |
| `app/admin/error.tsx` | Admin panel errors (reset + back to dashboard) |

## When

- Add segment `error.tsx` when a route group needs custom recovery (e.g. admin vs public).
- Use `reset()` for recoverable runtime errors.
- Pass `homeHref` / `homeLabel` for panel-specific escape paths.

## Pattern

```tsx
"use client";

import { ErrorPage } from "@/components/errors/error-page";
import { ROUTES } from "@/lib/constants/routes";

export default function SegmentError({ error, reset }) {
  return (
    <ErrorPage
      title="Something went wrong"
      description={error.message || "Please try again."}
      reset={reset}
      homeHref={ROUTES.ADMIN_DASHBOARD}
      homeLabel="Back to dashboard"
    />
  );
}
```

## Do not

- Build one-off error UIs per page — extend `ErrorPage` props if needed.
- Toast unhandled errors instead of showing the error page.
- Use `global-error.tsx` for segment-level errors — use `error.tsx` instead.
